{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken","id":1434234,"title":"Youngest Mage to Awaken","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-02T01:21:56-08:00","id":1434234,"title":"Youngest Mage to Awaken","content":"In the published material who was the youngest mage to awaken and how old were they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T01:39:41-08:00","id":1434235,"title":"","content":"They've said that children are born awakened but the vast majority go to sleep. Some very young children are awake, from the description, I assume four and five year olds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T01:46:05-08:00","id":1434237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434235#post1434235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've said that children are born awakened but the vast majority go to sleep. Some very young children are awake, from the description, I assume four and five year olds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Do any of them actually develop their powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T02:33:35-08:00","id":1434242,"title":"","content":"I seem to remember Dante (the Virtual Adept character) being stated to have awakened in the womb... or it might have been a vat (I think he was supposed to be a Technocrat project).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T04:36:20-08:00","id":1434250,"title":"","content":"IIRC the resolved version that cleaned up some of the early contradictions is that Dante was born naturally, but his mother died in childbirth and the Progenitors took over raising him, leading him to both remember being Awake in the womb, and being a Technocracy experiment; working with actual Progenitor created individuals that awakened and sought freedom thinking he had the same origin as them.<br /> <br /> In either case, it is the official stance that Dante Awakened before birth, and is the youngest mage in the books for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T07:41:57-08:00","id":1434257,"title":"","content":"<b>Book of Secrets</b> has a section on Child Mages that addresses this phenomenon: pp.115\u2013116. The opening paragraph starts with the premise that everyone is Awake in the womb, but most become Sleepers sometime after birth \u2014 presumably before they reach the toddler stage. A rare few, including Dante, never go to Sleep and have <i>always</i> been Awakened. If Dante is unique in that regard, is probably that he has <i>memories</i> from back then: most peoples' memories don't go back before 3 years old. <br /> <br /> So ultimately, the answer to the question is that there <i>isn't</i> a youngest age at which a mage Awakened, because the assumption that people started out Asleep and then had to Awaken turns out to be false. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, there's the flip side to this: if an Awakened infant can be lulled to Sleep, can the same happen to grown-ups? What would it take for a mage to <i>lose</i> Arete?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T10:01:39-08:00","id":1434266,"title":"","content":"So a naturally mystically sensitive 13 year old awakening with the right stimulus wouldn't be out of place. Neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T11:42:45-08:00","id":1434279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434257#post1434257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The opening paragraph starts with the premise that everyone is Awake in the womb, but most become Sleepers sometime after birth \u2014 presumably before they reach the toddler stage.</div> </div> </div> </div>The phrasing is more that everyone Awakens at birth than was already Awake then. Which is good because every human fetus being a mage would be a nightmare for the setting to try to deal with.<br /> <br /> Of course the start of that section is one of those really annoying old WW style things where it's written with all sorts of vague language that avoids saying if something is true or not in the setting (despite not being written from a clear in-character source to imply unreliable narrator), instead of discussing it as more of a dial for STs to use where how true it is can be played out. Then it treats it as true anyway for one paragraph, and then it doesn't actually matter to any of the rest of the discussion of child mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434266#post1434266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a naturally mystically sensitive 13 year old awakening with the right stimulus wouldn't be out of place. Neat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Such a character isn't out of place in the sense of being a phenomenon foreign to mages, but they'd still be a relative rarity, and face a lot of baggage (whether playing them from that point, or later as an adult mage that grew up with it). Young mages tend to have a lot of power to go with their lack of emotional development, and a lot of people want to decide for the child mage what's best for that power; including potential &quot;internal&quot; sources like past lives or an Avatar seeking a pliant mage to control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T12:37:16-08:00","id":1434282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434279#post1434279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The phrasing is more that everyone Awakens at birth than was already Awake then. Which is good because every human fetus being a mage would be a nightmare for the setting to try to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>The exact phrasing is: \u201c<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">According to certain philosophers, all infants are born Awakened and then get lulled to Sleep by the demands and structures of the human world.</span>\u201d Make of that what you will; my understanding of the phrasing is that it implies that they're already Awakened by the time they're born, not that the act of being born Awakens them. <br /> <br /> As for the difficulties of Awakened fetuses, I'm not particularly worried: \u201cAwakened\u201d and \u201cSleeper\u201d technically refer to the status of one's Avatar; but what that Avatar can do is largely channeled through its host's cognitive facilities; and infants generally don't have enough of those to <i>do</i> anything with the fact that they're Awakened until a good while <i>after</i> birth. Phrased another way: you need a Focus to work magick; and as a rule, most infants don't know enough about the world to form a Focus. So whether or not they're Awakened tends to be a moot point. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434279#post1434279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course the start of that section is one of those really annoying old WW style things where it's written with all sorts of vague language that avoids saying if something is true or not in the setting (despite not being written from a clear in-character source to imply unreliable narrator), instead of discussing it as more of a dial for STs to use where how true it is can be played out. Then it treats it as true anyway for one paragraph, and then it doesn't actually matter to any of the rest of the discussion of child mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The point is that there are characters who functionally were always Awakened, in that if they ever had a eureka moment where they came to realize that they had the power to change the world, it's not something they can recall: their memories simply don't go that far back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-02-2021, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T13:35:28-08:00","id":1434289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434279#post1434279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The phrasing is more that everyone Awakens at birth than was already Awake then. Which is good because every human fetus being a mage would be a nightmare for the setting to try to deal with.<br /> <br /> Of course the start of that section is one of those really annoying old WW style things where it's written with all sorts of vague language that avoids saying if something is true or not in the setting (despite not being written from a clear in-character source to imply unreliable narrator), instead of discussing it as more of a dial for STs to use where how true it is can be played out. Then it treats it as true anyway for one paragraph, and then it doesn't actually matter to any of the rest of the discussion of child mages.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Such a character isn't out of place in the sense of being a phenomenon foreign to mages, but they'd still be a relative rarity, and face a lot of baggage (whether playing them from that point, or later as an adult mage that grew up with it). Young mages tend to have a lot of power to go with their lack of emotional development, and a lot of people want to decide for the child mage what's best for that power; including potential &quot;internal&quot; sources like past lives or an Avatar seeking a pliant mage to control.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something I was a bit confused about. I was reading the wiki entry on Avatar and it says they are a natural part of the Mage, but then talks about them as if they are separate entity looking for a good match. Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T13:52:47-08:00","id":1434295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434282#post1434282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Phrased another way: you need a Focus to work magick; and as a rule, most infants don't know enough about the world to form a Focus. So whether or not they're Awakened tends to be a moot point.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Wild Magick?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T15:07:15-08:00","id":1434300,"title":"","content":"Wild Magick is the exception. It's also rare, outside of Marauders. It is, by definition, <i>not</i> something you can make happen. The one time when it's most likely to happen for a non-Marauder is during the Awakening; and I liken that to the Avatar breaking through a barrier and releasing the pent-up energy that was used to break through. With infants, there is no barrier and no pent-up energy, so no Wild Magick. Usually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T15:14:51-08:00","id":1434301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434289#post1434289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's something I was a bit confused about. I was reading the wiki entry on Avatar and it says they are a natural part of the Mage, but then talks about them as if they are separate entity looking for a good match. Am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether the Avatar is a natural pay of the mage or a separate entity is an open question, with evidence to support both views. The most likely explanation is that it's a natural pay of you; but it's usually a part that had a previous existence separate from your current existence; and that at some point, that previously separate thing became one of the building blocks in your nascent soul, making you \u201cyou\u201d. <br /> <br /> One form of child mage described is the exception to this: a <i>new</i> Avatar, with no prior existence. Such new Avatars start out with what amounts to True Faith, until such time as the world stomps it out of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T15:43:03-08:00","id":1434303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434282#post1434282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the difficulties of Awakened fetuses, I'm not particularly worried: \u201cAwakened\u201d and \u201cSleeper\u201d technically refer to the status of one's Avatar; but what that Avatar can do is largely channeled through its host's cognitive facilities; and infants generally don't have enough of those to <i>do</i> anything with the fact that they're Awakened until a good while <i>after</i> birth. Phrased another way: you need a Focus to work magick; and as a rule, most infants don't know enough about the world to form a Focus. So whether or not they're Awakened tends to be a moot point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before you even get to the magical capacity of fetuses and infants, there's the issue of their impact on Reality Zones/Consensus if they're Awakened and all they know is the womb and early sense memories. Even today, with vastly increased average lifespans meaning a lot more adults around, fetuses and infants make up one of the largest groups of people, with one of the most homogeneous cultural experience (that is, they have almost none). You do not have to go back in time very far for them to become a dominant force in shaping reality. That by itself is plenty of reason not to assume that the &quot;natural&quot; state of a human is Awakened and that they have to Sleep via early life experience.<br /> <br /> Then, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> notes, even if ~0.5% of Awakened fetuses demonstrate Wild Magic, that's still millions of Wild Magic using fetuses. On top of this are any of the potential influences that could result in more structured magic developing faster than a fetus should be able to by our real world understanding; a past life providing the Focus for example. No matter how rare any of this is, we are talking about, conservatively, around 750 million little Awakened beings out there between fetuses and infants on their way to falling Asleep.<br /> <br /> It's a mess of consequences that it's far easier to simply treat the idea as untrue than to try to work up an additional layer of setting assumptions to keep all of them in check.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point is that there are characters who functionally were always Awakened, in that if they ever had a eureka moment where they came to realize that they had the power to change the world, it's not something they can recall: their memories simply don't go that far back. </div> </div> </div>Agreed up until the memory part. That doesn't feel specified anywhere to me, and Dante the NPC exemplar of a character Awake in the womb is stated to have memories from before birth. While one could argue whether the beginning of his memories inherently came after his Awakening, or trust his subjective experience that it was a simultaneous event, it doesn't seem to be a core aspect of the narrative point of child mages that they can't remember that far back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434289#post1434289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's something I was a bit confused about. I was reading the wiki entry on Avatar and it says they are a natural part of the Mage, but then talks about them as if they are separate entity looking for a good match. Am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>The books are kind of all over the place on this. This was a big part of the Revised metaplot actually: Avatars are natural, but not inherent, to humans. When, exactly, they get attached isn't exactly specified, but everyone is supposed to get one. There is even a class of unique spirit that exists solely to perform this task. However, there was a break in the system, and instead of it being a seamless process where a mage's avatar was indistinguishable from the mage, the matching process started developing gaps, and avatars started developing unique identities related to their mages, but separate from them, which has been steadily getting worse esp. after the 15th Century when the spirits responsible for the process suddenly were barred from doing so and avatars started doing the process for themselves instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T17:48:09-08:00","id":1434311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434303#post1434303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a mess of consequences that it's far easier to simply treat the idea as untrue than to try to work up an additional layer of setting assumptions to keep all of them in check.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Adult Awakenings being a messy, traumatic, business (for countless supernatural reasons usualy tied to the Avatar) it's not that rare.<br /> <br /> As said, there are SO MANY Awakened if you count all fetuses, that even extemely rare supernatural problems would be more common among them than among regular mages - even if the chance it's lowered significatively. You would have to reduce the chance of these problems of Awakening to almost non-existence to justify this not being a <i>serious </i>issue.<br /> <br /> One could invent &quot;Avatars crashing barriers&quot; and whatnot to explain why Awakened fetuses <i>never </i>seem to have any problem. But I don't like to give so much of a special treatment. I don't want to invent a *different* (womb-only) type of Awakening to explain why fetuses are all mages, which it's in and of itself a bizarre idea.<br /> <br /> And I know very well where that idea comes from. It's from the popular idea that children are born without Banality and preconceptions. Castaneda had the idea that babies were able to *see* (the real Reality). It's not that rare.<br /> <br /> But do you <i>really</i> want to give them Arete/Spheres, potentially abusive Avatars, or other Mage stuff...for them to be able excert any of these capacities? Wouldn't be better to interpret babies being &quot;Awakened&quot; in the same vein as werewolves are &quot;Awakened beings&quot; - not counting as sleepers, yet not mages in any shape or form. <br /> Say babies have the Awareness Talent, then they *react* to magic because they can sense it. <br /> That should cover most of these beliefs that say babies are Awakened w/o the complications mages tend to bring to the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-02-2021, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T18:09:13-08:00","id":1434318,"title":"","content":"One potential consideration is Reality Zones. Most fetuses and infants live in the Consensus defined Reality Zone where they don't have any special spiritual or moral status. In Reality Zones dominated by other paradigms (such as babies born and raised in a Chantry), the idea that babies are special as filtered by the local Reality can then influence the truth of the idea. This would vastly reduce the number of fetuses and infants viable for more significant status as Awakened, and allows rarity to matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T18:47:24-08:00","id":1434328,"title":"","content":"In short, we already <i>have</i> two varieties of \u201cAwakened\u201d: one that involves mere awareness of the supernatural, and another that involves being able to actively influence it. I'll come back to this in a bit. <br /> <br /> The \u201cpunching through\u201d notion that I mentioned actually has nothing to do with babies, by the way; it's something I came up with a long time ago to explain why Wild Magick seems to coincide with Awakening, and rarely happens apart from that. When you asked about Wild Magick and Awakened fetuses, what immediately went through my mind was \u201cif the natural human state is Awakened, then there wouldn't be a moment of Awakening; and without a moment of Awakening, there wouldn't be that Wild Magick spike that accompanies it\u201d. Again, nothing specific being invented for the unborn. <br /> <br /> Now, I'm <i>not</i> picturing an unborn child as having Spheres, any more than it would have a Focus; its complete lack of any experiences precludes both. And that same lack of experiences means that it's not in a position to contribute to the Consensus; it doesn't have any belief system to contribute. All it gets is a couple of dots of Arete, which mostly do nothing except the rare one-dot \u201cWild Magick\u201d Effect \u2014 and nearly all one-dot Effects are sensory in nature, making this functionally equivalent to the \u201caware of the supernatural\u201d kind of Awakened. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> The other thing I'm thinking of here is how the Child Mage section talks about fresh Avatars coming with the functional equivalent of True Faith, and then rapidly losing it. I see a direct parallel between this and the idea that Avatars start out Awakened, but quickly go to Sleep. And in both cases, a similar thing is missing: a belief system to contextualize the Arete/Faith. Without a Paradigm (or a similar belief in a particular higher power, in the case of Faith), the Arete or Faith is unusually fragile and tends to disintegrate when brought into contact with harsh reality. In line with Heavy Arms' latest post, an infant raised in a Chantry or otherwise sheltered from harsh reality wouldn't face that same disintegration, at least not as fast, and would be better able to develop a Focus before ending up a Sleeper. <br /> <br /> (I also recall a section in the Revised Celestial Chorus TB that examined the relationship between Arete and True Faith; one of the possibilities it suggested is that they're <i>the same thing</i>; that Faith is \u201cmerely\u201d Arete coupled with a belief in a higher power. But I'm getting off track here.)<br /> <br /> Although the unborn children and infants would have Arete, I would not call them <i>mages</i>, because they lack nearly <i>everything else</i> that makes someone a mage; and their quick descent into Sleep illustrates exactly how important that missing Focus <i>is</i>. <br /> <br /> And it also suggests a possible avenues of research for the NWO when dealing with Superstitionists: is they could develop a technique, similar to Room 101 (or possibly as an <i>application of</i> Room 101) to shatter a mage's Focus \u2014 call all of her beliefs into question \u2014 could they maybe put her back to Sleep, and put the genie back in the bottle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-02-2021, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T18:58:18-08:00","id":1434332,"title":"","content":"Basically, I'm seeing four categories: <br /> <br /> \u2022 Sleepers have neither Arete nor Focus. <br /> \u2022 Mages have both. <br /> \u2022 Extraordinary Citizens and their mystical counterparts have Focus, but not Arete. <br /> \u2022 Arete without Focus is possible, but unstable: you either develop a Focus and become a mage, or you lose the Arete and become a Sleeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T19:02:51-08:00","id":1434333,"title":"","content":"My main consideration would be: What's the advantage of saying all fetuses are functionaly mages?<br /> <br /> I could see it in a mystical setting, where some babies are born with the strength of Heracles, others are taken by their Manifest Avatars, some have wisdom beyond their age...etc.<br /> <br /> But if one starts by looking all the more or less handwavey excuses to stomp any and all Mage weirdness out of the babies...<br /> <br /> ...I fail to see the advantage over saying Awakened (as in, Arete wielding) babies are rare, but exist. And perhaps babies and little kids tend to be very Aware and that's why they see ghosts, react to magic, and whatnot...and that's what &quot;many beliefs&quot; call being Awakened in it's most basic form","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-02-2021, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T19:55:08-08:00","id":1434337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434333#post1434333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main consideration would be: What's the advantage of saying all fetuses are functionaly mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beats me; I'm not saying that. There's nothing functional about them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434333#post1434333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see it in a mystical setting, where some babies are born with the strength of Heracles, others are taken by their Manifest Avatars, some have wisdom beyond their age...etc.<br /> <br /> But if one starts by looking all the more or less handwavey excuses to stomp any and all Mage weirdness out of the babies...</div> </div> </div> </div>I have provided <i>one</i> justification (<i>not</i> an excuse), and it is decidedly <i>not</i> handwavey: no one that young, and with virtually no life experiences, can form a coherent Focus. No Focus, no Magick. Simplicity itself. Everything beyond that is just details. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434333#post1434333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I fail to see the advantage over saying Awakened (as in, Arete wielding) babies are rare, but exist. And perhaps babies and little kids tend to be very Aware and that's why they see ghosts, react to magic, and whatnot...and that's what &quot;many beliefs&quot; call being Awakened in it's most basic form</div> </div> </div> </div>Six of one, half a dozen of the other. Both approaches have the same outcome. One does so entirely within <b>Mage</b>'s metaphysics, and suggests other implications that could be explored (such as the notion of shattering a Focus to put a mage to Sleep); the other treats the notion of Awakened infants as a special case that exists largely <i>outside of</i> <b>Mage</b>'s metaphysics, and as such has about as much to say about <b>Mage</b> as <b>Changeling</b> does. <br /> <br /> The latter also outright dismisses something in print, while the former embraces it. As you know, I'm not shy about rejecting stuff that's in print if I think it's problematic; for instance, my whole stance on Earthly Foundations that I've argued several times now is basically a rejection of the idea that the true, objective reality of <b>Mage</b> is that it's purely subjective. But whenever I do so, I first try to see if I can get what's there to work as is; and if I can't, <i>then</i> I make the <i>smallest</i> changes I can to achieve workable results. <br /> <br /> In this case, I don't think changes are needed; just clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-02-2021, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T05:19:16-08:00","id":1434371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434337#post1434337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have provided <i>one</i> justification (<i>not</i> an excuse), and it is decidedly <i>not</i> handwavey: no one that young, and with virtually no life experiences, can form a coherent Focus. No Focus, no Magick. Simplicity itself. Everything beyond that is just details.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't apply to ANY of my objections.<br /> <br /> No Focus = No <i>Sphere Magick.</i><br /> <br /> It doesn't preclude Backgrounds, Merits and Defects or Wild Magick. The core of my objections it's that *being a mage* can come with a lot of baggage that has nothing to do with actually casting spells.<br /> <br /> And let's keep in mind that something &quot;being rare&quot; means very little with the amount of babies there are in the world.<br /> <br /> And about the more or less handwavey stuff:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In Reality Zones dominated by other paradigms (such as babies born and raised in a Chantry), the idea that babies are special as filtered by the local Reality can then influence the truth of the idea. This would vastly reduce the number of fetuses and infants viable for more significant status as Awakened, and allows rarity to matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adults get to be &quot;special&quot; in supernatural ways the Consensus does not aprove off, while babies don't for some reason? Or you need your mage to Awaken in a specific kind of Reality Zone to manifest specific Backgrounds, Merits and Defects or Wild Magic?<br /> <br /> Think that depending on your backstory certain Backgrounds (like having past lives providing a Focus, as you suggested) or Merits and Defects may not be apropiate for mages unless they Awakened in very issolated and special places (i.e Orphans most likely can't access them - least you risk babies in huge demographic areas to be born with powers) - if significant status as Awakened depends on the Zone<br /> <br /> I think this is fine - it may even help to maintain &quot;the masquerade&quot; better (in general) - but also I think it's stretching the rules of RZ to justify something I'm not convinced needs to be true.<br /> <br /> But I think maybe I didn't got your point here...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">All it gets is a couple of dots of Arete, which mostly do nothing except the rare one-dot \u201cWild Magick\u201d Effect \u2014 and nearly all one-dot Effects are sensory in nature, making this functionally equivalent to the \u201caware of the supernatural\u201d kind of Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, this is a good example of handwave. What is this &quot;the rare one-dot Wild Magick Effect&quot;?<br /> <br /> <i>Why ONE dot?</i><br /> <br /> The rule I *think* you may be refering to, where M20 *suggests* the ST to give a mage one <i>or two </i>more Sphere dots to cast an effect it's a special variation of the Wild Magic rule intended to be used when a character dies (it's an optional rule) . It's ruled so players can invoque it willingly to cause a desired effect...it's a very special case<br /> <br /> But that's not the general rule of Wild Magic.<br /> <br /> Read the general rule of Wild Magic: &quot;the wild talent phenomenon manifests through intense stress, pain, trauma,<b> or</b> brand-new Enlightenment...Unlike the previous entries, wild talent is not a Sphere. Rather, it\u2019s a plot device that represents uncontrolled (and uncontrollable) currents of Awakened energy. The mage in question has awareness without understanding...For a scene or two, <b><i>she commands an Arete dice pool that\u2019s one, two, or perhaps three dice higher than usual; employs Spheres she might not understand; and may access Sphere Ranks 3, 4, or even 5 </i></b>if the Storyteller so desires.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also: &quot;even if ~0.5% of Awakened fetuses demonstrate Wild Magic, that's still millions of Wild Magic using fetuses&quot; - Heavy Arms<br /> <br /> But also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cif the natural human state is Awakened, then there wouldn't be a moment of Awakening; and without a moment of Awakening, there wouldn't be that Wild Magick spike that accompanies it\u201d. Again, nothing specific being invented for the unborn.<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> All it gets is a couple of dots of Arete, which mostly do nothing except the rare one-dot \u201cWild Magick\u201d Effect \u2014 and nearly all one-dot Effects are sensory in nature, making this functionally equivalent to the \u201caware of the supernatural\u201d kind of Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>1\u00b0 Fetuses DO or DON'T get to cause Wild Magic?<br /> <br /> You can't have it both ways.<br /> <br /> If they don't, then you can't really mimic Awareness with that. If they do...well, I would rather go with that they don't and give them real Awareness instead, because you really don't wan't fetuses using RAW wild magic.<br /> <br /> 2\u00b0<br /> The rule says: &quot;the wild talent phenomenon manifests through intense stress, pain, trauma,<b> OR </b>brand-new Enlightenment&quot; - &quot;has awareness without understanding&quot; fits these babies perfectly.<br /> <br /> So you still need to &quot;outright dismiss something in print&quot;, after all, to have it so Awakened babies *don't* cause Wild Magic. Still the best option by a mile<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The other thing I'm thinking of here is how the Child Mage section talks about fresh Avatars coming with the functional equivalent of True Faith, and then rapidly losing it. I see a direct parallel between this and the idea that Avatars start out Awakened, but quickly go to Sleep. And in both cases, a similar thing is missing: a belief system to contextualize the Arete/Faith. Without a Paradigm (or a similar belief in a particular higher power, in the case of Faith), the Arete or Faith is unusually fragile and tends to disintegrate when brought into contact with harsh reality. In line with Heavy Arms' latest post, an infant raised in a Chantry or otherwise sheltered from harsh reality wouldn't face that same disintegration, at least not as fast, and would be better able to develop a Focus before ending up a Sleeper. </div> </div> </div>I'm quite missing your point here.<br /> <br /> These things may be similar, but I don't see the relation - &quot;fresh&quot; Avatars are Avatars that belonged to no one else before, Avatars that haven't reincarnated yet. I'm not sure how these giving Faith for some reason has anything to do with babies being Awakened. You can put two and two together, sure...but do you need to?<br /> <br /> Also, I see a dangerous implication with the latter point:<br /> <br /> If the Reality Zone heavily influences the dissolution of the Focusless Arete then raising babies in a Realm or Chantry it's a sure way to heavily increase the chance of having more mages. That way you can &quot;mass produce&quot; mages - this is a BIG deal, one that mage factions can't ignore<br /> <br /> And it's something mages had to have to observed in Realms, since these are often the home of many Acolites that have children.<br /> <br /> The opportunity to educate mages from scratch in big numbers it's simply too valuable. One would think this &quot;sheltering&quot; of children would be as important for mages as for Garou it's to mate propperly, if the ratio of developping a Focus before ending up a Sleeper <i>does </i>increaase significatively. Odd such an important rule of thumb never gets mentioned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The latter also outright dismisses something in print </div> </div> </div>Care to mention that part I'm dismissing?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">The &quot;According to certain philosophers...</span></span>&quot; in no way or fashion it's making a reference to the rules or the canon. If anything, I'm dismissing what &quot;certain philosophers&quot; say.<br /> And even then that's not entirely true. Mage uses the Awakening word two ways, as you stated, so maybe they weren't thinking about being a <s>mage</s> - sorry, I meant a<i>&quot;non mage Arete wielder that doesn't get to have any mage mechanic other than Arete and, perhaps, one dot of wild magic given Spheres (and never more than one dot)&quot;</i> - but in a more holistic definition of the word<br /> <br /> I would like if you could quote the wording I'm actually dismissing, to see if it's so important as to deserve this many &quot;clarifications&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-03-2021, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T08:07:22-08:00","id":1434385,"title":"","content":"&quot;Certain philosophers say that we're all born Awakened&quot; seems to be mostly a poetic, aspirational statement that informs character worldview than something to be treated as totally literal to deconstruct under the microscope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T10:46:17-08:00","id":1434401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434371#post1434371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think maybe I didn't got your point here...</div> </div> </div> </div>My point here is more of a compromise position: whether or not &quot;humans are born Awakened and become Sleepers in infancy,&quot; is true is local Reality dependent rather than a constant. If it's not part of Consensus, than our shared issue with the hundreds of millions of fetuses and infants on Earth is a non-issue, as only a tiny fraction of humanity lives in a sufficiently different Reality Zone, and not all of them are going to be different on this issue.<br /> <br /> This could in fact make pregnancies in such RZs rather dangerous since most children would still end up Sleepers, but you'd still have to risk a few years (starting before birth) of them doing random magic just for them to lose it (also not running in a mage-factory issue) by the time they could start to be taught more structured magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434385#post1434385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Certain philosophers say that we're all born Awakened&quot; seems to be mostly a poetic, aspirational statement that informs character worldview than something to be treated as totally literal to deconstruct under the microscope.</div> </div> </div> </div>As noted earlier in the thread, part of the problem is that the discussion of &quot;born mage&quot; child mages treats the aspirational statement as a true statement in its description of such characters, mucking with the ability to take it as mere poetic license.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T12:39:40-08:00","id":1434411,"title":"","content":"I'm at work right now, so can't do an in-depth response to anything. But a quick note: what I'm trying to do here isn't to take a side as it were. It's to explore the possibility that the \u201ccertain philosophers\u201d may be right, rather than just assuming that they're wrong.<br /> <br /> I will give a more in-depth response this evening, when I have time to sit down and look things over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T06:23:12-08:00","id":1434482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434401#post1434401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point here is more of a compromise position: whether or not &quot;humans are born Awakened and become Sleepers in infancy,&quot; is true is local Reality dependent rather than a constant. If it's not part of Consensus, than our shared issue with the hundreds of millions of fetuses and infants on Earth is a non-issue, as only a tiny fraction of humanity lives in a sufficiently different Reality Zone, and not all of them are going to be different on this issue.<br /> <br /> This could in fact make pregnancies in such RZs rather dangerous since most children would still end up Sleepers, but you'd still have to risk a few years (starting before birth) of them doing random magic just for them to lose it (also not running in a mage-factory issue) by the time they could start to be taught more structured magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, I was missing the point by quite a lot.<br /> <br /> I'm OK with that position. That does answer all my objections satisfactorily.<br /> <br /> Humm...even in RZs there probably aren't so many pregnancies as to make rare issues like babies possesed by Past Lives, or fetuses wielding Wild Magic, a serious problem (unless some crazy mage starts to try my &quot;mass production of mages&quot; schemes - and then, well, that mage will reap what he sow).<br /> <br /> Now I imagine those philosophers ain't fond of the Technocratic reality. And also that, if faced with such romantic notions, the protectors of &quot;...<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">the demands and structures of the - </span>current<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"> - human world</span>...&quot; could come up with an argument similar to my own arguments to explain why it's good that the Consensus supresses being Awakened in the womb.<br /> <br /> And I can't call it much of a handwave when it's using a soft mechanic that's supposed to work that way, perhaps even implied to work that way, even if it isn't called out explicitly by the BoS. I don't have any argument that would make &quot;awakening&quot; or &quot;not awakening&quot; a Cosmologial Constant or Foundation, so I guess the Consensus could be altering that posibility and that's why the complications that naturaly come with Awakening aren't common<br /> <br /> If we generalize to adults the way I did before, it fits with the Tradition's idea that Awakenings were more common in the past (which it's something I always thought as kinda necessary, because the demographics of, say, DA wouldn't allow for many cabals of mages if mages were as rare as they're supposed to be in the modern era). And Awakened fetuses being more common in the past could be the source of tales and legend that speak about such &quot;special&quot; cases as babies talking like old people and such.<br /> <br /> I'm liking this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-04-2021, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T07:06:02-08:00","id":1434490,"title":"","content":"Having said this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't call it much of a handwave when it's using a soft mechanic that's supposed to work that way, perhaps even implied to work that way, even if it isn't called out explicitly by the BoSI don't have any argument that would make &quot;awakening&quot; or &quot;not awakening&quot; a Cosmologial Constant or Foundation, so I guess the Consensus could be altering that posibility and that's why the complications that naturaly come with Awakening aren't common</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like I have to add that I won't accept an appelation to the Consensus to diminish the chance or potency of Wild Magic and other bizarre Awakened shenanigans.<br /> <br /> The reason why I won't accept that it's that <s>mages</s> <i>Arete wielders</i> are <i>supposed </i>to be able to act against the Consensus. All their kit it's supposed to be able to do so, with consequences. That's why magick (and the supernatural) <i>exists</i>. And, let's face it, pregnancies are complicated enough without adding Orphan Wild Magic Paradoxes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T08:16:58-08:00","id":1434493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434411#post1434411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm at work right now, so can't do an in-depth response to anything. But a quick note: what I'm trying to do here isn't to take a side as it were. It's to explore the possibility that the \u201ccertain philosophers\u201d may be right, rather than just assuming that they're wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may give a couple of suggestions for your explorations:<br /> <br /> 1\u00b0<br /> Don't just gloss over Heavy Arm's argument about how common are fetuses/babies/small children vs mages. This is important because a LOT of the Mage setting it's bassed uppon how rare it's the Awakened state. Lot's of small things put together can mean a lot.<br /> <br /> 2\u00b0<br /> Unless you're intending the make a *third* Awakened state (one for the Aware, one for the Mage and a third one for the infant), you have to aknowledge that the mechanics of the Awakened babies are going to be the same as those of the mage (because you've already discarded the Aware). Or give a coherent explanation about why the mechanics of the adult should be different when their &quot;Awakened state&quot; it's not.<br /> <br /> I *can* accept, for instance, that babies aren't going to have Spheres - reluctantly, though, because Orphans often get points in Spheres without any specific study or teaching. But I could get behind the idea that Orphan Spheres are, say, formed as a coalescence of their current understanding of the world as adults caused by the spark of genius - fetuses are still developping sentience so there's nothing to &quot;build&quot; the Spheres uppon. Or something on those lines. This is already a hard stance on something Mage leaves open. But OK, that's what game theories are.<br /> <br /> I can totally accept babies aren't going to have a Focus. I would argue anyone that would suggest otherwise...<br /> <br /> ...my only objection with doubling down too hard on this it's that the Child Mage section leaves oppen the idea that small children are also ALL Awakened (in line how in other gamelines small children can se ghosts, fae, etc...the whole &quot;innocent children&quot; trope). But Focus it's a sufficently vage concept for even the smallest children to have it on some capacity. Small children that know even a few words already have stong Beliefs (often stronger than those of their parents) - you may argue that these &quot;aren't complex enough to form a Focus&quot;, but that's debatable and leaves you in a much weaker stance to counter<i> Heavy Arms</i> argument about these billons of Awakened not affecting the Consensus - needing to grab onto the idea that babies have no Focus it's, thus a bit unsatisfactory to me. If only because it requires humans to go Sleep before learning how to speak, and I'm not sure that was the intention of that &quot;aspirational&quot; passage - I want to quote Borges here in saying Language it's a form of minor magic...<br /> <br /> I *can't* accept that argument at all for Wild Magic or powerful and problematic Avatars causing potent Echoes, possesing vivid Past Lives, or in general producing paranormal phenomena . When the very, very, few adults that Awaken have chances to have so many problems coming with &quot;being Awakened&quot;, it' simply too much to assume it's always going to end well for babies (and if you're thinking: well, it' doesn't *always* go well, please go back to point 1\u00b0).<br /> <br /> 3\u00b0<br /> If babies are going to be Awakened in the same sense as Mages are Awakened - don't be silly and complain when I call them mages. There's this thing called context, and in the context it's a preposterous thing to &quot;clarify&quot;.<br /> <br /> Obviously when I say you're proposing &quot;all fetuses are mages&quot;, I'm not saying you're proposing to make them start with 6 dots in Spheres and chose a faction in the Ascencion War. I'm not an idiot. I'm saying you're proposing all fetuses start with the basic elements of the &quot;mage splat&quot; ruleset (fetuse's hypothetical &quot;character sheet&quot; would have Arete, wheel of Quintessence, Awakened Avatar with an Essence, etc...obviously stuff like &quot;how many dots&quot; may vary, Focus it's left empty until they get one, etc).<br /> <br /> Because that specific definition<i> <b>only</b></i><i><b> applies to mages</b></i> in the canon (prove me wrong), I'm allowed to say &quot;Mages&quot; instead of &quot;The Awakened&quot;. <i>The books *often* use these as sinonimous.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-04-2021, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T14:33:55-08:00","id":1434531,"title":"","content":"It should also be noted that the rules for making child mages explicitly give them: Arete 2 and 6 dots of Spheres, and an Affinity Sphere (which they're free to pick any rather than being bound by a faction's set).<br /> <br /> This applies to any child mages, as the rules do specify other things that only apply to some child mages (including things like developmental stages, not just supernatural factors).<br /> <br /> I would also say that I'd be very cautious about getting into neural development as it relates to the ability to form a Focus. There is a large difference between a Focus that's been refined to be functional on the level of what's assumed to be base-line for normal mages, and what an unrefined Focus that works well enough for some magic to be performed look like, and what level of development would be seen as necessary to form such thoughts.<br /> <br /> I would posit that the core basis of the whole concept of Paradigms/Focuses is the human brain's pattern recognition system, because its the foundation of how we learn about the world, and build our understanding of the world. It's a part of our brain that develops in utero, because as a matter of survival we need to start sorting stimuli into patterns, and start to correlate patterns to each other. A case against very young child mages having enough of a Focus to perform magic has to be more nuanced than just &quot;they can't possibly have one yet,&quot; because we know that it's possible to have an &quot;immature&quot; Focus that is less practical that the one's presented for PCs by default, that can grow into something closer to what's a normal Focus with time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T15:58:53-08:00","id":1434536,"title":"","content":"Not strictly relevant, but a mage I ran in a D&amp;D game (Amber d\u2019Ambreville) Awakened at 13 and reached 9th level by the time she was 18.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T19:17:04-08:00","id":1434552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434531#post1434531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would posit that the core basis of the whole concept of Paradigms/Focuses is the human brain's pattern recognition system, because its the foundation of how we learn about the world, and build our understanding of the world. It's a part of our brain that develops in utero, because as a matter of survival we need to start sorting stimuli into patterns, and start to correlate patterns to each other. A case against very young child mages having enough of a Focus to perform magic has to be more nuanced than just &quot;they can't possibly have one yet,&quot; because we know that it's possible to have an &quot;immature&quot; Focus that is less practical that the one's presented for PCs by default, that can grow into something closer to what's a normal Focus with time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather like your notion of maturity of Foci (side note: M20 capitalizes it, earlier editions don't; so I personally use the case to indicate whether or not I'm talking M20's take on it). In this case, when I say \u201cno Focus\u201d, I don't mean <i>literally</i> none; I mean that any Focus they have is too \u201cimmature\u201d to have any use as a way to focus Magick. While I'm no expert on child development, I'm pretty sure that most infants haven't gotten to the point where they can assemble what <b>Mage</b> considers to be a Focus: a working theory about how the world works (the Paradigm; \u201cEverything is Data\u201d, \u201cTechnology Hold All the Answers\u201d, and so on) and some sort of approach to leveraging that into practical results (the Practice; Alchemy, Medicine Work, etc.). I could <i>maybe</i> see something like Everything is Chaos as the default Paradigm (though I tend to associate that more with an <i>active rejection</i> of the alternatives than as a default belief structure); but every Practice I can think of requires more experience than an infant has. <br /> <br /> That's why I'm arguing that Awakened infants and fetuses wouldn't have a working Focus. And without that, they would have no way to use any Spheres that they might happen to have, barring only Wild Talent. The point where they develop a sophisticated enough Focus to Willwork would almost certainly come after the point when they'd normally start retaining memories. (It's entirely possible that Heavy Arms is right with his theory that being Awakened <i>causes</i> you to retain memories, perhaps in the form of the Avatar retaining them for you; but I wouldn't take that as a given.)<br /> <br /> <b>Initiates of the Art</b> starts a newly-Awakened mage with Arete 1 and two Spheres, the idea being that the core book's starting mage has already had some time to acclimate. The fact that a child mage starts with six dots in Spheres makes me think that a similar premise is in play there: the assumption isn't that the child mage has just Awakened; is that he's been Awake for a while now, and doing things that have helped develop his Magickal comprehension of the world. Indeed, the core of thrusts debate is centered around this that section suggests that may have <i>always</i> been Awakened. An Awakened infant would be more like the Apprentice, if even <i>that</i> far developed: at <i>most</i> two Spheres, maybe one or even none. And again: until a functional Focus is developed, having Spheres doesn't mean much. Likewise with Willpower: starting mages have 5; but newly-Awakened mages only have 3, the same as Sleepers. I could see arguments for sharing that infants might be even weaker than that, on the average; possibly as low as 1 or 2. <br /> <br /> The Arete 2 bothers me a bit, as I like to think of Arete as how refined your Focus is; and Child Mages having a higher Arete than adults contradicts that. But that's what the section says, so I'm more inclined to go with it than to toss it out. Perhaps a better way to think of it would be as a sort of Magickal finesse; more like an Attribute than an Ability; and how refined the Focus is might be better represented by an appropriate Ability (e.g., Esoterica or Science). <br /> <br /> Backgrounds are also most likely to be almost entirely nil for the car majority of infants, let alone fetuses; only a handful, like Avatar or Past Lives, stand a chance of having <i>any</i> sort of rating; so the vast majority of Awakened infants aren't likely to have any Backgrounds. Merits and Flaws that you either have or don't will be there all along; but there aren't that many of those that actually matter in terms of the distinction between Sleeper and Awakened. <br /> <br /> Abilities are right out; even Talents are something you develop with practice, and infants are still at the point where they're struggling to grasp language and basic mobility. And while the Child Mage section says that you must take the \u201cChild\u201d and \u201cShort\u201d Flaws, I think that even they aren't up to the task of representing the difficulties that an infant faces. <br /> <br /> In short (no pun intended), an infant is too underdeveloped to be represented on a standard character sheet. They're missing so much of what it takes to be a playable character that there's really no point. I bring this up only because of the argument that they somehow ought to have Backgrounds, Merits, and so on, should they happen to be Awakened. I can see the argument that they shouldn't even be able to be Awakened at that stage of development; but the <b>Book of Secrets</b> suggests otherwise, so that's what I'm going with. <br /> <br /> Finally, one more issue I have with saying that \u201cthey're Awakened by the time they're born\u201d refers to the <i>other</i> kind of Awakened: it still suggests that the Child Mage transitioned to the Mage-style Awakened state from some other state, whereas the <b>Book of Secrets</b> implies that those who have always been Awakened have always been Mage-style Awakened. That's why I'm not inclined to explain away the \u201calready Awakened when born\u201d notion with a different kind of Awakened, and why I'm instead leaning heavily into the \u201cMage-style Awakened, but not yet developed enough to do anything with it\u201d approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T00:43:41-08:00","id":1434563,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting, IMO, that children having a good Focus isn't necessarily a contradiction - if anything, children would potentially have less problem 'accepting' a set of paradigms and belief, as they are in that age bracket where nature pretty much intends them to soak up information being taught to them.<br /> <br /> *And* they have the uncanny ability to somehow put everything they pick up into some kind of worldview that makes sense. Possibly *only* to them, but the only thing a proper Focus requires *is* for it to make sense in the Mage's head. In that regard, I would sprinkle the Focus of a child-mage with a certain kind of dream-logic, where there are some pieces and things that would maybe make an adult blink a bit in confusion. As they get older, the Focus 'matures' a bit as well, but as long as the focus makes *sense* to the child, it...works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T01:58:23-08:00","id":1434571,"title":"","content":"I'm suddenly imagining that a touch of magic could inform some of the uncanny things that accompany earliest childhood, but parents can't make sense of it or mess it up with a spot of Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T03:51:44-08:00","id":1434575,"title":"","content":"The idea of child Mages starting with an Arete of two is about the idea that Child Mages have far less to unlearn. It is influenced by Romantic and mystical views of early childhood. To quote Blake, &quot;to see infinity in a grain of sand/ and Heaven in a wildflower.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T04:12:05-08:00","id":1434579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434552#post1434552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Backgrounds are also most likely to be almost entirely nil for the car majority of infants, let alone fetuses; only a handful, like Avatar or Past Lives, stand a chance of having <i>any</i> sort of rating; so the vast majority of Awakened infants aren't likely to have any Backgrounds. Merits and Flaws that you either have or don't will be there all along; but there aren't that many of those that actually matter in terms of the distinction between Sleeper and Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>But those handful that you mention are the ones that cause problems with this whole idea (and perhaps also Dream, Arcane...supernatural stuff that require little to no world interaction).<br /> <br /> A babie could have a Mentor, too, but who cares?...I care more about Avatar stuff, the capabilities, Backgrounds, Merits and Defects that come with having one of these wide Awake. Because this has 0 to do with development and all to do with being Awakened. A mage being an adult, a child or a babie would have rougly the same soul, wouldn't it?. And when that comes with stuff like Echoes 5 (to put an example)...well, that's one complicated childhood.<br /> <br /> Now, a few of these rare &quot;problematic&quot; Avatars won't make or break the setting, but when ALL fetuses are Awakened suddenly having a child increases one's chance to be exposed to paranormal phenomena quite a lot. That's why I'm more inclined to go with a vision that, at least, supresses this factoid in <i>most </i>cases.<br /> <br /> And about Focus: As I said, debatable. I'm inclined to go with the &quot;no, there's no way. A Focus isn't just belief, it's a whole philosophy that also includes persistent Practice&quot; - but Mage Childs seem to be inclined to disagree with the motion, since they're shown as having what I would ordinarily call very undevelopped Focuses if I didn't know better. So, debatable.<br /> <br /> But I don't think having Focus without Spheres (or with lvl 1 Spheres as per Initiates) would do much anyway. That's more a problem with the - very complex-ramifications of your theory, than with the idea itself. That's why I'm more concerned with the Wild stuff.<br /> <br /> If all little children are Awakened and have &quot;belief&quot;, however, even without a Focus that could suffice to be a force in the Consensus - I'm mentioning this for<i> Heavy Arms</i> first objection &quot;. You do not have to go back in time very far for them to become a dominant force in shaping reality&quot;. I hadn't tought much about that originaly because, as you said, fetuses and babies have noting of value to aport to the Consensus (except, maybe, reinforcement for the Foundations from early experience). But with little children in mind, one could have to reconsider that idea...<br /> ...Maybe that's why Technocracy can't get rid of the monsters :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-05-2021, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T04:13:47-08:00","id":1434580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434575#post1434575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of child Mages starting with an Arete of two is about the idea that Child Mages have far less to unlearn. It is influenced by Romantic and mystical views of early childhood. To quote Blake, &quot;to see infinity in a grain of sand/ and Heaven in a wildflower.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, of course. That whole section is a tribute to those ideas.<br /> <br /> Another reason of why I'm more inclined to go with <i>Heavy Arms</i> version now, preferring it to my own previous proposition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T07:00:02-08:00","id":1434593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434579#post1434579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But those handful that you mention are the ones that cause problems with this whole idea (and perhaps also Dream, Arcane...supernatural stuff that require little to no world interaction).<br /> <br /> A babie could have a Mentor, too, but who cares?...I care more about Avatar stuff, the capabilities, Backgrounds, Merits and Defects that come with having one of these wide Awake. Because this has 0 to do with development and all to do with being Awakened. A mage being an adult, a child or a babie would have rougly the same soul, wouldn't it?. And when that comes with stuff like Echoes 5 (to put an example)...well, that's one complicated childhood.<br /> <br /> Now, a few of these rare &amp;quot;problematic&amp;quot; Avatars won't make or break the setting, but when ALL fetuses are Awakened suddenly having a child increases one's chance to be exposed to paranormal phenomena quite a lot. That's why I'm more inclined to go with a vision that, at least, supresses this factoid in <i>most </i>cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>My inclinations is to say that the demographics of adult mages doesn't apply to Awakened infants: just because, say, one in a hundred adult mages has Avatar-related complications doesn't mean that one in a hundred Awakened infants do. Remember, the vast majority of these infants are going to go to Sleep before long. And most of those are unlikely to ever Awaken after they go to Sleep. The ones with\u2026 complicated Avatars are, in both cases, likely to be the exceptions; in particular, the Child Mages section cites a handful of Backgrounds that they're likely to have, which could be taken as \u201cif you have one of these Backgrounds, you're less likely to go to Sleep and more likely to Awaken of you do\u201d \u2014 and as such, these Backgrounds are more likely to be found in Child Mages. <br /> <br /> But again, <i>most</i> infants will have \u201cordinary\u201d Avatars, without the likes of an Avatar or Past Lives Background, or any of the Supernatural Merits or Flaws; and <i>those</i> infants get lulled to Sleep before they're old enough to be viable characters. As for them having an excessive influence on the Consensus, that's where their underdeveloped Foci factor in: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434579#post1434579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And about Focus: As I said, debatable. I'm inclined to go with the &amp;quot;no, there's no way. A Focus isn't just belief, it's a whole philosophy that also includes persistent Practice&amp;quot; - but Mage Childs seem to be inclined to disagree with the motion, since they're shown as having what I would ordinarily call very undeveloped Focuses if I didn't know better. So, debatable.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's \u201cunderdeveloped\u201d, and then there's \u201cI don't even know how to walk or talk\u201d. I'm not finding the page reference right now; but M20 has a section in it talking about how not all Foci are created equal, and that you need a Paradigm that's robust enough to tackle the issues of the world around you if you're going to be successful as a Mage. I'd say that this holds for Child Mages, too, with the caveat that they tend toward the more simplistic end of what's considered to be a viable Paradigm; but when you get to infants and fetuses, the vast majority simply aren't even in the same ballpark as \u201cviable Focus\u201d. If a robust Focus is a ten-speed bike, the sorts of Foci that Child Mages tend toward would be more like tricycles; and the sports of Foci that fetuses and infants would have would be a <i>box of bicycle parts, not yet assembled</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1434234-youngest-mage-to-awaken?p=1434579#post1434579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If all little children are Awakened and have &amp;quot;belief&amp;quot;, however, even without a Focus that could suffice to be a force in the Consensus - I'm mentioning this for<i> Heavy Arms</i> first objection &amp;quot;. You do not have to go back in time very far for them to become a dominant force in shaping reality&amp;quot;. I hadn't tought much about that originaly because, as you said, fetuses and babies have nothing of value to aport to the Consensus (except, maybe, reinforcement for the Foundations from early experience). But with little children in mind, one could have to reconsider that idea...<br /> ...Maybe that's why Technocracy can't get rid of the monsters :P</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, I'm drawing a distinction between \u201clittle children\u201d and \u201cinfants\u201d. I could see \u201clittle children\u201d being a force in the Consensus, if not for the fact that most of them have already gone to Sleep by that point. Infants, by contrast, have \u201csome assembly required\u201d Foci, and for the most part are more likely to be affected <i>by</i> the Consensus than to affect it. Which is why most of them end up going to Sleep. <br /> <br /> I'll get back to you on the Wild Talent bit. I have some thoughts on that, but I need to do some research before I can present them properly. It involves a short story written by science fiction author David Brin; I believe it was in a book he wrote called <i>Otherness</i>, and it features an expectant mother who's dealing with what amounts to Progenitors experimenting on her unborn child. It has a very Mage-like ending. But I don't have the book handy right now, and I want to refresh my memory before I go any further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}